  "name": "Backfill versie_id from manually-linked Versions",
  "description": "No-code reverse of \"Match taken-versie records\" (wflpsJp2NjbxYeSgf): when a Taken record already has a Versions link (e.g. linked manually in the UI, not via the Nieuwe taak form) but no versie_id, find that same Versions record via its own recordId formula field and copy its recordIdVersion (the Assets-base record ID) into Taken.versie_id. Keeps versie_id populated as a permanent cross-base trace regardless of how the Taken/Versie link was made -- the Assets base's \"Link task to versions\" automation (wflLEzbMBJHdbtukc) depends on versie_id being set to build its reciprocal Versies -> Taken link. Only handles the single-linked-Versie case -- guarded on the trigger record's OWN Versions link count (fixed 2026-08-14: an earlier version of this guard incorrectly checked the findRecords match count instead, which is always 1 regardless of how many Versies are linked, and mis-processed one multi-Versie Taken by silently using only its first link).",
